winedmo: Convert large video frames with libswscale's slice threading.

Proton-GE's winedmo backend decodes on several threads but converts every
frame (for example YUV to BGRA for the Media Engine) with sws_scale() on the
calling thread, then copies it. Valve's winegstreamer runs videoconvert with
n-threads=0 (all cores). For high-resolution pre-rendered video the
single-threaded conversion is a bottleneck that Valve's path does not have.

Use a scaler context created with the "threads" option and sws_scale_frame()
for frames of 1280x720 and larger. Any failure falls back permanently, for
that transform, to the existing single-threaded path.

Written for EX-Proton. Applies after Proton-GE's patch set and
patches/wine/0001.

--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -87,6 +87,10 @@
     /* Video output conversion */
     SwsContext         *sws;
     AVFrame            *sws_frame;       /* padded scaler output, copied to the caller's buffer */
+    SwsContext         *sws_mt;          /* multi-threaded scaler for large frames */
+    AVFrame            *sws_mt_src;      /* reference to the input frame, cropped to the visible size */
+    int                 sws_mt_params[7];
+    bool                sws_mt_failed;   /* fall back to the single-threaded scaler */
     enum AVPixelFormat  out_pix_fmt;     /* AV_PIX_FMT_NONE = native */
